Feature: Vehicle commands
  ARM needs a second press to confirm it. For a plane, [[home]] is the point where you arm
  it, and [[RTL]] brings the plane back to that point. The mode buttons change the flight
  mode of ArduPilot. If the vehicle has no mission, AUTO asks you to confirm, because the
  plane would go to RTL immediately.

  Expectation: Arming sets home
    If the button shows ARM: NOT READY, wait. ArduPilot does its pre-arm checks first, and
    the button shows ARM when they pass.
    Given the vehicle is disarmed
    And the link is connected
    When the operator arms the vehicle
    Then the vehicle is armed
    And the home position is set

  Expectation: DISARM disarms
    Given the vehicle is armed
    When the operator disarms the vehicle
    Then the vehicle is disarmed

  Expectation: AUTO flies the vehicle's mission
    Given the vehicle mission is not empty
    When the operator switches to AUTO
    Then the autopilot mode is AUTO
    And the vehicle's current item is 1

  Expectation: AUTO with no mission asks first
    If you did not upload a mission, AUTO would go to RTL immediately. Thus the button
    changes to AUTO: NO MISSION?, and the MESSAGES screen tells you why. To change to AUTO,
    press the button again in four seconds or less.
    Given the vehicle mission is empty
    When the operator switches to AUTO
    Then the autopilot mode stays the same

  Expectation: AUTO twice goes anyway
    Given the vehicle mission is empty
    When the operator switches to AUTO anyway
    Then the autopilot mode is AUTO

  Expectation: In AUTO, a throw starts the mission
    With the physics of the sim, the takeoff waits for a [[hand launch]]. The HUD of the sim
    says "AUTO takeoff: throw it (SPACE or B)". The motors start after the throw.
    Given the autopilot mode is AUTO
    And the vehicle is armed
    And the plane is on the ground
    When the pilot throws the plane in the sim
    Then the plane is flying the mission
